ese does not mark part of speech, so this is not a part-of-speech error.\n- A usage note in brackets such as （表示…）, alongside an equivalent or in place of one.\nfail when any of these holds:\n- It means something else, or any listed equivalent is wrong for this sense, even when a bracketed note explains the usage correctly.\n- For a verb sense, an equivalent only names a thing or quality and cannot be used as a verb.\n- It renders a phrase or phrasal verb that contains the word instead of the word in this sense.\n- It renders a different sense of the word, such as one of the other senses listed below.\n- It is unnatural or ungrammatical in the target language.\n- It lists equivalents of several unrelated senses.\nOther senses of this entry, for reference:\n- (adjective) \"Having a high temperature or a temperature higher than is comfortable.\"\n- (adjective) \"Served at a high temperature after being heated or cooked.\"\n- (adjective) \"Recent enough to provide promising clues about someone or something being sought.\""}},"context":{"subject":{"lemma":"hot","pos":"adjective","gloss":"Very close to finding a hidden object or guessing the correct answer in a game.","siblings":[{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Having a high temperature or a temperature higher than is comfortable."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Served at a high temperature after being heated or cooked."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Recent enough to provide promising clues about someone or something being sought."}]},"target":null,"topic":null},"reviewed_at":"2026-11-09T23:23:52.239Z"}', '2026-11-09T23:23:41.510Z', '2026-11-09T23:23:52.239Z', 'zh');
