that part of speech.\n- It renders a phrase or phrasal verb that contains the word instead of the word in this sense.\n- It renders a different sense of the word, such as one of the other senses listed below.\n- It is unnatural or ungrammatical in the target language.\n- It lists equivalents of several unrelated senses.\nOther senses of this entry, for reference:\n- (noun) \"An animal that lives in water, breathes through gills, and has fins.\""}},"context":{"subject":{"lemma":"fish","pos":"verb","gloss":"To try to catch fish.","siblings":[{"pos":"noun","gloss":"An animal that lives in water, breathes through gills, and has fins."}]},"target":null},"reviewed_at":"2026-11-09T08:56:46.417Z"}', '2026-11-09T08:56:38.445Z', '2026-11-09T08:56:46.417Z', 'zh');
