earners use that preposition after the word in this sense, as a learner''s dictionary writes it (\"rely on/upon sb/sth\", \"good at sth\").\npass: every claim holds for this sense. Patterns and prepositions are the common ones a learner needs, not all of them: a pattern or preposition left out is not an error.\nfail: any claim is wrong for this sense or holds only for another sense, a pattern is rare or unnatural with this sense, or a named preposition is not the one learners use with this sense or is rare with it.\nOther senses of this entry, for reference:\n- (noun) \"An animal kept for companionship or pleasure.\"\n- (noun) \"A person who receives special affection or preferential treatment from someone.\"\n- (adjective) \"Receiving special personal interest, attention, or affection.\"\n- (verb) \"To kiss and caress someone in a sexual way.\"\n- (noun) \"A kind or lovable person, especially one addressed affectionately.\""}}}]},"context":{"subject":{"lemma":"pet","pos":"verb","gloss":"To stroke or touch an animal gently and affectionately.","siblings":[{"pos":"noun","gloss":"An animal kept for companionship or pleasure."},{"pos":"noun","gloss":"A person who receives special affection or preferential treatment from someone."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Receiving special personal interest, attention, or affection."},{"pos":"verb","gloss":"To kiss and caress someone in a sexual way."},{"pos":"noun","gloss":"A kind or lovable person, especially one addressed affectionately."}]},"target":null,"topic":null},"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10T05:16:22.380Z"}', '2026-11-10T05:16:16.942Z', '2026-11-10T05:16:22.380Z', '');
